#   Comments + Keyword Clarification

#    Anton, Calculus, 4.5.20
# DESCRIPTION
# Given perimeter constraint, determine the measurements of a box that generates the greatest volume.

# ENDDESCRIPTION
## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Applications of differentiation)
## DBsection(Optimization - general)
## Institution(John Wiley & Sons)
## MLT(USPSgirth)
## Level(5)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Anton')
## EditionText1('9')
## Section1('4.5')
## Problem1('20')
## KEYWORDS('Functions', 'Applied Problems', 'Maximize', 'Perimeter', 'Volume', 'Optimization')
DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'contextFraction.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

#    Restrictions on box:
#       1)  It has a square base (side S) and vertical sides (H)
#       2)  Perimeter of lateral side + width <= $A
#            2S + 2H + S = $A  ==>  H = ($A - 3S)/2

#       Volume = (S^2)H = S^2($A - 3S)/2

#       V'(S) = (2$AS - 3S^3)/2  ==> = 0 at S = (2/9)A   (Make A a multiple of 9)
Context("Numeric")->variables->add(S => 'Real', H => 'Real');

$A      = random(108, 180, 9);
$Side   = Formula("2*$A/9")->reduce;
$Volume = Formula("$Side^2*($A - 3*$Side)/2")->reduce;

$Vprime = Formula("(2*$A S - 9 S^2)/2")->reduce;
$VofS   = Formula("($A S^2 - 3 S^3)/2");
$Vsub   = $VofS->substitute(S => $Side);

BEGIN_PGML
A box with a square base is wider than it is tall. In order to send the box through the U.S. mail, the width of the box and the perimeter of one of the (nonsquare) sides of the box can sum to no more than [$A] in. What is the maximum volume for such a box?  

    Maximum Volume = [_]{$Volume} [`\textrm{in}^3`]
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
If we refer to the length of a side of the base as [` S`] and the height as [` H`], then
the volume of the box is,
[``` V = S^2H.```]

The perimeter of one of the nonsquare sides of the box would be [` 2S + 2H`], and using the constraint
that the sum of the width [`(S)`] and this perimeter be no more than [$A] inches, we have,
[``` 3S + 2H = [$A], \;\mbox{or}\; H = \frac{[$A] - 3S}{2}.```] 

Substituting this into the equation for volume we have,
[``` V = S^2\left(\frac{[$A] - 3S}{2}\right) \; \mbox{or} \; V = [$VofS].```]

To find the maximum volume, differentiate and set equal to 0:
[``` V\;'(S) = [$Vprime] \quad \Rightarrow V\;'(S) = 0\; \mbox{when} \;S = [$Side] \; \mbox{in}```]
To find the corresponding volume,
[``` V = \frac{[$A] ([$Side])^2 - 3 ([$Side])^3}{2} = [$Volume] \;\mbox{in}^3.```]

END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
